REQUIRES: arm-registered-target

Windows CE compressed .pdata: lld resolves the internal FUNCLEN/PROLOG
pseudo relocations (IMAGE_REL_ARM_CE_PDATA_FUNCLEN/PROLOG) into the flags
word, compacts each 16-byte intermediate object record to the 8-byte
IMAGE_CE_RUNTIME_FUNCTION_ENTRY layout (pFuncStart, flags), sorts by
pFuncStart (the CE kernel binary-searches, RtlLookupFunctionEntry), and
reports the compact size in the exception data directory.

Flags word bitfields (exdsptch.c:42-48, verified against real CE images
in utils/wince/WINEH-ABI-FACTS.md):
  PrologLen:8 | FuncLen:22 | ThirtyTwoBit:1 | ExceptionFlag:1
Lengths are in instructions (InstSize = 2 for Thumb, 4 for ARM).
pFuncStart is the image-relative (RVA) function start; Thumb functions
carry the Thumb marker in bit 0.

RUN: llvm-mc -triple thumb-pc-wince -filetype=obj -o %t.second.o %S/Inputs/wince-pdata-second.s
RUN: llvm-mc -triple thumb-pc-wince -filetype=obj -o %t.first.o %S/Inputs/wince-pdata-first.s
RUN: lld-link /out:%t.exe /subsystem:windowsce /entry:second /base:0x10000 /fixed %t.second.o %t.first.o

## Linked .text (RVA 0x1000):
##   +0x00 __C_specific_handler (2B)
##   +0x02 second's PDATA_EH pair (8B)
##   +0x0A second (4 Thumb instructions, 8B)
##   +0x12 first's PDATA_EH pair (8B)
##   +0x1A first (3 Thumb instructions, 6B)
##
## pFuncStart = RVA + Thumb bit: second 0x100B, first 0x101B.
## flags: ExceptionFlag | FuncLen<<8 | PrologLen:
##   second 0x80000401, first 0x80000301.

The exception directory must report the compacted 8-byte-per-entry size:
2 entries * 8 = 0x10.

RUN: llvm-readobj --headers %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HDR
HDR:      ExceptionTableRVA: 0x2000
HDR-NEXT: ExceptionTableSize: 0x10

.pdata after compaction and sort, ascending by pFuncStart:
  [second 0x100B, 0x80000401] [first 0x101B, 0x80000301]

RUN: llvm-objdump -s --section=.pdata %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PDATA
PDATA:      Contents of section .pdata:
PDATA-NEXT: 12000 0b100000 01040080 1b100000 01030080
